[{"answer":"Today we're going to begin with a short quiz.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/1.mp3"},{"answer":"No, no, you don't need pencil and paper, just listen.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/2.mp3"},{"answer":"It's only one question.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/3.mp3"},{"answer":"Ready? OK.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/4.mp3"},{"answer":"What do blogs, Pokemon, tattoos, Cabbage Patch Kids, pet rocks, and hula hoops have in common?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/5.mp3"},{"answer":"Anybody?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/6.mp3"},{"answer":"They're all stupid.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/7.mp3"},{"answer":"I know, Professor Morgan. They're all fads.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/8.mp3"},{"answer":"Correct.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/9.mp3"},{"answer":"Now here's another question:","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/10.mp3"},{"answer":"How did you know that?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/11.mp3"},{"answer":"In other words, what are the characteristics of a fad,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/12.mp3"},{"answer":"and what's the difference between a fad and a trend?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/13.mp3"},{"answer":"These are the questions we're going to consider together this afternoon.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/14.mp3"},{"answer":"Well, the main difference, I think, between a fad and a trend concerns time.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/15.mp3"},{"answer":"A fad is something that seems to appear suddenly.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/16.mp3"},{"answer":"It quickly becomes enormously popular,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/17.mp3"},{"answer":"then disappears just as suddenly as it came.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/18.mp3"},{"answer":"A trend also appears rather suddenly,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/19.mp3"},{"answer":"and it also becomes very popular,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/20.mp3"},{"answer":"but it doesn't disappear.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/21.mp3"},{"answer":"A trend can have a long-term influence on its particular market.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/22.mp3"},{"answer":"Fads and trends often resemble each other at first glance,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/23.mp3"},{"answer":"but a fad usually has a definite beginning and end.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/24.mp3"},{"answer":"Um, Pokemon might be a fad,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/25.mp3"},{"answer":"but the idea of fancy playing cards for children might be a trend, for example.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/26.mp3"},{"answer":"Another difference is that fads usually stay within one industry.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/27.mp3"},{"answer":"Trends can cross over into many industries.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/28.mp3"},{"answer":"The hula hoop, for instance, has been called the greatest fad of all time.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/29.mp3"},{"answer":"25 million...","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/30.mp3"},{"answer":"In the late 1950s, 25 million hula hoops were sold in just four months.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/31.mp3"},{"answer":"But a year later, sales had virtually stopped.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/32.mp3"},{"answer":"The hula hoop was a toy.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/33.mp3"},{"answer":"It was fun to play with, but that's about all.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/34.mp3"},{"answer":"Now consider cell phones.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/35.mp3"},{"answer":"They were designed to be portable telephones,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/36.mp3"},{"answer":"but they crossed over into the worlds of fashion,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/37.mp3"},{"answer":"wireless communication, and now even photography.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/38.mp3"},{"answer":"People buy cell phones that match the latest clothes fashions.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/39.mp3"},{"answer":"They use cell phones for wireless Internet access.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/40.mp3"},{"answer":"They take photos with them.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/41.mp3"},{"answer":"Cell phones have become a trend.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/42.mp3"},{"answer":"Here's the third difference between fads and trends:","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/43.mp3"},{"answer":"how well industries accept them.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/44.mp3"},{"answer":"Fads are often promoted by smaller companies.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/45.mp3"},{"answer":"They need the quick money that fads provide.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/46.mp3"},{"answer":"Large companies don't accept fads right away.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/47.mp3"},{"answer":"They can't afford to be wrong.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/48.mp3"},{"answer":"If a company is known as a trend-setter,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/49.mp3"},{"answer":"and it promotes a fad, its reputation will be damaged.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/50.mp3"},{"answer":"Large companies buy products in huge numbers.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/51.mp3"},{"answer":"They don't want unsold products sitting on their shelves.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/52.mp3"},{"answer":"So they wait to see if a fad becomes a trend.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/53.mp3"},{"answer":"Then they will accept it in their stores.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/54.mp3"},{"answer":"Now... yes?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/55.mp3"},{"answer":"How long does a fad have to last before it becomes a trend?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/56.mp3"},{"answer":"I mean, there are all these energy drinks now.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/57.mp3"},{"answer":"There used to be only a couple, but now there's like, a hundred.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/58.mp3"},{"answer":"Are they still a fad?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/59.mp3"},{"answer":"Exercise is a trend, so wouldn't energy drinks be part of the exercise trend?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/60.mp3"},{"answer":"That's an excellent question!","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/61.mp3"},{"answer":"When exactly does a fad become a trend?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/62.mp3"},{"answer":"You know, there are some people who are paid a lot of money to answer that question.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/63.mp3"},{"answer":"If they get it right, companies become rich and famous.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/64.mp3"},{"answer":"If they get it wrong, companies go bankrupt and careers get ruined.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/65.mp3"},{"answer":"The short answer is: nobody knows.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/66.mp3"},{"answer":"Distinguishing between fads and trends is an art, not a science.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/67.mp3"},{"answer":"If it were easy, there would be a lot more rich people in the world.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/68.mp3"},{"answer":"Yes, in the back.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/69.mp3"},{"answer":"Yeah, um... can't people get rich from fads, too?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/70.mp3"},{"answer":"You said they sold 25 million hula hoops in four months.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/71.mp3"},{"answer":"Someone must have made big money off that?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/72.mp3"},{"answer":"Yes, they did.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/73.mp3"},{"answer":"Toy companies made, uh, $45 million off of hula hoops by the time the fad ended.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/74.mp3"},{"answer":"And maybe some of you have heard of pet rocks, in the 1970s?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/75.mp3"},{"answer":"A man bought a rock for a penny,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/76.mp3"},{"answer":"put it in a gift box and marketed it as a pet.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/77.mp3"},{"answer":"He became an instant millionaire.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/78.mp3"},{"answer":"But the problem... the trouble with fads is,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/79.mp3"},{"answer":"no one can predict them.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/80.mp3"},{"answer":"This man had no idea that so many people would buy rocks as pets.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/81.mp3"},{"answer":"He started it as kind of a joke.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/82.mp3"},{"answer":"The Pokemon creators had no clue their cards would become instantly popular all over the world.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/83.mp3"},{"answer":"That's the thing.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/84.mp3"},{"answer":"Fads are mysterious to both their creators and to the public.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/toefl-listening/lecture-2-2023-01-13-22-57-52/85.mp3"}]
